    "suggestion": "One specific missing edge-case test for the Python game verifier could be:\n\n1. **Invalid Move Count**: The game verifier does not check if the move count is valid. It only checks if the move count is at least 2 and up to 5. However, the move count should be between 2 and 5, inclusive. Therefore, a test could be:\n\n```python\ndef simulate(seed):\n    default = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / \"build\" / \"balance\"\n    result = subprocess.run([os.environ.get(\"ATLAS_ORACLE\") or str(default), str(seed), str(MOVES), str(PANES)], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True, timeout=5)\n    return json.loads(result.stdout)\n```\n\nThis test",
